{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeBraidingSubstrateNonSymmetric","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HeckeBraidingSubstrateNonSymmetric","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.HeckeBraidingNonSymmetric","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.TraceSignFlipRegime"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeBraidingSubstrateNonSymmetric.trace_not_sign_flip_invariant_of_q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HeckeBraidingSubstrateNonSymmetric.trace_not_sign_flip_invariant_of_q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeBraidingSubstrateNonSymmetric.lean#L49-L75","doc":"**The trace tower is not sign-flip invariant at the substrate.**\n\n`rem:isospin-mass-split-em-localisation` lists the trace tower among the\nfunctionals that *\"respect these structural involutions\"*, and uses that to\nlocalise the mirror-isobar mass split entirely into the Coulomb sector. At any\nreal `q > 1` — the substrate included — this says the premise is false for that\nsector: flipping a generator's sign changes the trace.\n\nThe remark's cited support, `prop:crystal-isospin-degeneracy`, is a **crystal\nlimit `q → 0`** statement, and remains true there. Both facts hold; what does not\nhold is carrying the `q → 0` invariance across to the functional at `q₀`. The\nsize of the failure is `(q − q⁻¹) · tr 1`, about `0.209 · tr 1` at\n`q₀ ≈ 1.10998`, so it is not a negligible-correction argument either.\n\nScope-(a), and narrow: this refutes one premise for one sector at one regime. It\ndoes not touch the co-Casimir or chirality sectors, and it does not refute the\nremark's conclusion — the split may still be entirely Coulomb-sourced. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeBraidingSubstrateNonSymmetric.q_gt_one_double_braiding_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HeckeBraidingSubstrateNonSymmetric.q_gt_one_double_braiding_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeBraidingSubstrateNonSymmetric.lean#L32-L47","doc":"**Archimedean corollary** (the wall is crossed here, and only here: `ℝ`\nappears because the substrate value is a real number, per §7c).\n\nAt any real `q > 1` the double braiding is not the identity. The substrate sits\nat `q₀ ≈ 1.10998`, so the QOU braiding is non-symmetric — which is what the\naudit needs, and it is a consequence of the Hecke relation rather than a\nstipulation. ","signatureChunk":0}]}